From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 14 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] blink: do not add a second fallthrough after gperf 3.3

  at_rule_descriptors.cc:133:7: error: fallthrough annotation does not
  directly precede switch label

gperf used to emit only a /*FALLTHROUGH*/ comment, and gperf.py turned it into
a real statement for -Wimplicit-fallthrough
(https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/index.php?53029). gperf 3.3 fixed that bug: it
now emits its own properly guarded annotation and still leaves the comment, so
the substitution produces two annotations in a row and the first no longer
precedes a case label. Blink is generated with gperf-native, which is 3.3 on
wrynose, so every generated CSS table failed to build.

Drop the comment and let gperf's own annotation stand.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/third_party/blink/renderer/build/scripts/gperf.py
+++ b/src/third_party/blink/renderer/build/scripts/gperf.py
@@ -34,11 +34,15 @@
         # it from gperf's output.
         # https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/index.php?53028
         gperf_output = re.sub(r'\bregister ', '', gperf_output)
-        # -Wimplicit-fallthrough needs an explicit fallthrough statement,
-        # so replace gperf's /*FALLTHROUGH*/ comment with the statement.
-        # https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/index.php?53029
-        gperf_output = gperf_output.replace('/*FALLTHROUGH*/',
-                                            '  [[fallthrough]];')
+        # gperf used to emit only a /*FALLTHROUGH*/ comment, which this script
+        # turned into a real statement for -Wimplicit-fallthrough
+        # (https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/index.php?53029). gperf 3.3 fixed that
+        # bug and now emits its own properly guarded annotation, while still
+        # leaving the comment behind, so substituting here produces two
+        # annotations in a row and the first no longer precedes a case label:
+        #   error: fallthrough annotation does not directly precede switch label
+        # Just drop the comment and let gperf's own annotation stand.
+        gperf_output = gperf_output.replace('/*FALLTHROUGH*/', '')
         # -Wpointer-to-int-cast warns about casting pointers to smaller ints
         # Replace {(int)(long)&(foo), bar} with
         # {static_cast<int>(reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(&(foo)), bar}
